WEBVTT

00:00:26.110 --> 00:00:29.884
I can't believe we
actually bought this thing.

00:00:29.917 --> 00:00:32.523
There's a reason charity
auctions have an open bar.

00:00:32.556 --> 00:00:34.460
Don't you think...

00:00:34.493 --> 00:00:36.597
I don't know, it's kind of creepy?

00:00:38.701 --> 00:00:40.672
It's okay.

00:00:40.705 --> 00:00:43.178
I'll keep you safe.

00:00:44.280 --> 00:00:46.617
Maybe you're the one i
ought to be scared of.

00:00:48.688 --> 00:00:51.794
Mmm. Let's go upstairs.

00:00:51.828 --> 00:00:54.934
Give me 10 minutes to lock up.

00:00:54.967 --> 00:00:56.838
Mmm.

00:00:56.871 --> 00:00:58.373
Make than one minute.

00:01:48.006 --> 00:01:51.314
If you don't hurry up, i'm
gonna start without you!

00:02:11.486 --> 00:02:14.293
Babe, get the lights.
I can't see a thing.

00:02:20.504 --> 00:02:22.275
Do you smell something?

00:02:23.911 --> 00:02:25.415
Ann?

00:02:28.086 --> 00:02:29.622
Ann?!

00:02:48.227 --> 00:02:50.832

...3-4-2-0.

00:02:51.901 --> 00:02:53.971
All right. You're in there.

00:02:54.005 --> 00:02:55.107
Perfect.

00:02:55.140 --> 00:02:57.879
So, is that brandi with a "y" or an "i"?

00:03:15.415 --> 00:03:18.454
All right, listen. I got to go.

00:03:18.488 --> 00:03:20.592
Hold that thought. I'll
be right back, okay?

00:03:22.661 --> 00:03:25.301
All right, so, i think i got
something. Oh, yeah, me too.

00:03:25.335 --> 00:03:27.271
I think we need to take
a little shore leave

00:03:27.305 --> 00:03:29.343
For just a little bit.
What do you think, huh?

00:03:29.376 --> 00:03:31.012
I'm so in the door with this one here.

00:03:31.045 --> 00:03:33.451
So, what are we today,
dean? Are we rock stars?

00:03:33.484 --> 00:03:34.785
Are we army rangers?

00:03:34.820 --> 00:03:37.492
We're l.A. Tv scouts looking
for people with special skills.

00:03:38.594 --> 00:03:40.632
But, hey, it's not that far off, right?

00:03:40.664 --> 00:03:43.371
By the way, she's got
a friend over there.

00:03:43.404 --> 00:03:45.240
I can probably hook you
up. What do you think?

00:03:45.274 --> 00:03:47.011
Dean, uh, no thanks.
I can get my own dates.

00:03:47.044 --> 00:03:49.115
Yeah, you can, but you don't.

00:03:49.148 --> 00:03:51.186
What is that supposed to mean?

00:03:51.219 --> 00:03:52.923
Nothing. What do you got?

00:03:52.956 --> 00:03:55.495
Mark and ann telesca
of new paltz, new york,

00:03:55.528 --> 00:03:58.601
Were both found dead in their
home just a few days ago.

00:03:58.634 --> 00:04:00.471
Throats were slit, there were no prints,

00:04:00.505 --> 00:04:02.274
No murder weapons, all
- Dean?

00:04:02.308 --> 00:04:03.578
No prints, no murder weapons,

00:04:03.611 --> 00:04:05.582
All doors and windows were
locked from the inside.

00:04:05.615 --> 00:04:07.686
Could just be a garden-Variety murder.

00:04:07.718 --> 00:04:10.023
You know, not our department.
No, dad says different.

00:04:10.057 --> 00:04:11.092
What do you mean?

00:04:11.125 --> 00:04:12.094
Look.

00:04:12.127 --> 00:04:13.296
Dad noted three murders

00:04:13.330 --> 00:04:15.234
In the same area of upstate new york.

00:04:15.267 --> 00:04:17.805
First one, right here, 1912.

00:04:17.838 --> 00:04:21.614
The second one in 1945,
and the third in 1970.

00:04:21.647 --> 00:04:24.185
The same m.O. As the telescas
- The throats were slit,

00:04:24.218 --> 00:04:25.989
The houses were locked from the inside.

00:04:26.022 --> 00:04:27.559
So much time passed between the murders

00:04:27.592 --> 00:04:29.395
That nobody checked the
pattern except for dad.

00:04:29.429 --> 00:04:31.433
He always kept his eyes
peeled for another one.

00:04:31.467 --> 00:04:32.801
And now we got one. Exactly.

00:04:32.835 --> 00:04:35.040
All right. I'm with you.
It's worth checking out.

00:04:35.073 --> 00:04:37.311
We can't pick this up till
first thing, though, right?

00:04:37.344 --> 00:04:39.650
Yeah. Good.

00:04:39.683 --> 00:04:41.152
Dean...

00:04:41.185 --> 00:04:42.622
Ladies. Did you miss me?

00:04:42.656 --> 00:04:44.325
I'm just kidding.

00:04:44.358 --> 00:04:47.197
Listen, i talked to my
producer, and it is looking good.

00:05:03.698 --> 00:05:05.601
Oh, man, that's so not cool.

00:05:05.635 --> 00:05:09.108
I just swept the telesca
house with the emf. It's clean.

00:05:09.141 --> 00:05:11.780
And last night, while you were...

00:05:11.814 --> 00:05:13.049
Out...

00:05:13.083 --> 00:05:14.385
Oh, good times.

00:05:14.418 --> 00:05:16.055
...i checked the history of the house.

00:05:16.089 --> 00:05:17.692
No hauntings, no violent crimes,

00:05:17.726 --> 00:05:20.230
Nothing strange about the
telescas themselves, either.

00:05:20.263 --> 00:05:22.569
So if it's not the people
and it's not the house,

00:05:22.602 --> 00:05:24.171
Then maybe it's the contents -

00:05:24.205 --> 00:05:26.376
A cursed object or
something. House is clean.

00:05:26.409 --> 00:05:27.779
You said that.

00:05:27.812 --> 00:05:28.814
No, i mean it's empty.

00:05:28.848 --> 00:05:30.852
No furniture, nothing.

00:05:30.884 --> 00:05:33.189
Where's all their stuff?

00:06:01.279 --> 00:06:04.385
Silent auctions, estate sales -

00:06:04.418 --> 00:06:07.056
It's like a garage sale for
w.A.S.P.S, if you ask me.

00:06:07.089 --> 00:06:08.426
Can i help you, gentlemen?

00:06:11.097 --> 00:06:13.970
I'd like some champagne, please.

00:06:14.003 --> 00:06:15.741
He's not a waiter.

00:06:19.381 --> 00:06:22.321
I'm sam connors.

00:06:22.354 --> 00:06:24.960
This is my brother, dean.

00:06:24.992 --> 00:06:27.129
We are art dealers with connors limited.

00:06:27.164 --> 00:06:29.100
You're art dealers? That's right.

00:06:29.133 --> 00:06:31.539
I'm daniel blake. This
is my auction house.

00:06:31.572 --> 00:06:34.746
Now, gentlemen, this
is a private showing,

00:06:34.779 --> 00:06:37.685
And i don't remember seeing
you on the guest list.

00:06:37.719 --> 00:06:39.020
We're there, chuckles.

00:06:39.053 --> 00:06:41.225
You just need to take another look.

00:06:41.259 --> 00:06:42.661
Oh, finally.

00:06:45.200 --> 00:06:46.469
Cheers.

00:07:04.572 --> 00:07:07.779
A fine example of american
primitive, wouldn't you say?

00:07:13.389 --> 00:07:16.696
Well, i'd say it's more
grant wood than grandma moses

00:07:18.333 --> 00:07:19.769
But you knew that.

00:07:19.803 --> 00:07:21.439
You just wanted to see if i did.

00:07:21.472 --> 00:07:23.276
Guilty.

00:07:23.309 --> 00:07:25.982
And clumsy. I apologize.

00:07:26.015 --> 00:07:27.952
I'm sarah blake.

00:07:27.986 --> 00:07:30.557
I'm sam.

00:07:30.590 --> 00:07:35.033
This is my...brother, dean.

00:07:35.066 --> 00:07:36.469
Dean. Hmm.

00:07:36.502 --> 00:07:38.138
Can we get you some more mini quiche?

00:07:38.171 --> 00:07:40.710
Mnh-Mnh, i'm good. Thanks.

00:07:40.744 --> 00:07:43.181
So, can i help you with something?

00:07:43.215 --> 00:07:45.553
Yeah, actually.

00:07:45.587 --> 00:07:48.426
What can you tell us
about the telesca estate?

00:07:48.459 --> 00:07:50.630
The whole thing's pretty
grisly if you ask me,

00:07:50.664 --> 00:07:52.634
Selling their things this soon.

00:07:52.668 --> 00:07:54.772
But dad's right about one thing -

00:07:54.805 --> 00:07:57.044
Sensationalism brings out the crowds.

00:07:57.077 --> 00:07:59.515
Even the rich ones.

00:08:02.319 --> 00:08:04.391
Is it possible to see the provenances?

00:08:04.425 --> 00:08:08.231
I'm afraid there isn't
any chance of that.

00:08:08.265 --> 00:08:10.235
Why not?

00:08:10.269 --> 00:08:11.839
You're not on the guest list...

00:08:11.873 --> 00:08:13.409
And i think it's time to leave.

00:08:13.443 --> 00:08:15.447
Well, we don't have to be
told twice. Apparently, you do.

00:08:15.480 --> 00:08:16.515
Okay, it's all right.

00:08:16.549 --> 00:08:19.421
We don't want any trouble. We'll go.

00:08:26.635 --> 00:08:28.606
Dad, that was rude.

00:08:31.512 --> 00:08:33.951
Grant wood, grandma moses
- What?

00:08:33.984 --> 00:08:35.319
Art history course.

00:08:35.352 --> 00:08:36.923
It's good for meeting girls.

00:08:36.957 --> 00:08:38.760
It's like i don't even know you.

00:08:55.794 --> 00:08:56.896
Huh.Huh.

00:08:56.929 --> 00:08:59.101
And what was the providence?

00:08:59.134 --> 00:09:00.236
Provenance.

00:09:00.270 --> 00:09:01.705
It's a certificate of origin,

00:09:01.739 --> 00:09:03.075
Like a biography, you know?

00:09:03.109 --> 00:09:05.345
We can use them to track
the history of the pieces,

00:09:05.379 --> 00:09:07.083
See if anything's got a freaky past.

00:09:07.117 --> 00:09:09.453
We're not getting
anything out of chuckles,

00:09:09.488 --> 00:09:10.924
But, uh, sarah... yeah.

00:09:10.957 --> 00:09:12.828
Maybe you can get her
to write it on a napkin.

00:09:12.861 --> 00:09:14.264
Not me.

00:09:14.298 --> 00:09:15.667
Oh, no, no, no, no.

00:09:15.700 --> 00:09:17.369
Pickups are your thing, dean.

00:09:17.403 --> 00:09:19.541
It wasn't my butt she was checking out.

00:09:19.575 --> 00:09:22.881
In other words, you want me
to use her to get information.

00:09:22.914 --> 00:09:24.450
Sometimes you got to
take one for the team.

00:09:24.483 --> 00:09:26.989
Call sarah.

00:09:31.332 --> 00:09:32.767
Nice place.

00:09:32.801 --> 00:09:33.903
Yeah.

00:09:42.287 --> 00:09:43.388
Glad you called.

00:09:44.457 --> 00:09:46.629
Surprised, but glad.

00:09:46.662 --> 00:09:47.697
Yeah?

00:09:47.731 --> 00:09:49.533
Although you seemed to have a hard time

00:09:49.568 --> 00:09:51.939
Getting out the words, "would
you like to have dinner?"

00:09:51.972 --> 00:09:54.043
Yeah.

00:09:54.077 --> 00:09:57.250
I haven't really been
on a date in a while.

00:09:57.284 --> 00:09:58.719
Welcome to the club.

00:09:58.753 --> 00:10:01.191
You're kidding me.

00:10:01.225 --> 00:10:04.998
Man: here we are.

00:10:05.032 --> 00:10:06.635
The wine list.

00:10:20.062 --> 00:10:24.805
I don't know about romeo
here, but i'll have a beer.

00:10:27.109 --> 00:10:28.145
And you?

00:10:28.179 --> 00:10:29.480
I will, too.

00:10:29.513 --> 00:10:30.549
Certainly.

00:10:30.582 --> 00:10:32.921
Sam: so, you studied art in school, huh?

00:10:32.954 --> 00:10:33.990
Sarah: it's true.

00:10:34.023 --> 00:10:35.092
I was an artist -

00:10:35.125 --> 00:10:39.066
A terrible, terrible artist.

00:10:39.100 --> 00:10:41.070
That's why i'm in the auction business.

00:10:41.104 --> 00:10:42.606
And you were pre-Law?

00:10:42.639 --> 00:10:43.709
Yeah.

00:10:43.743 --> 00:10:46.715
But you didn't go to
law school. How come?

00:10:46.749 --> 00:10:50.456
Uh, it's a really long
story for another time.

00:10:50.490 --> 00:10:53.094
You're not like any art
dealer i've ever met.

00:10:58.205 --> 00:11:00.510
So...what did you mean when you said

00:11:00.542 --> 00:11:02.179
You hadn't been on a date in a while?

00:11:02.213 --> 00:11:03.949
Trying to make me feel
like i'm not such a loser?

00:11:03.983 --> 00:11:05.685
I'm sure many things, sam.

00:11:05.720 --> 00:11:08.859
I'm also sure "loser" isn't one of them.

00:11:13.769 --> 00:11:15.973
It was my mom.

00:11:16.007 --> 00:11:18.245
She died about a year ago.

00:11:18.279 --> 00:11:20.850
Totally unexpected.

00:11:22.787 --> 00:11:24.324
It really threw me.

00:11:26.027 --> 00:11:31.704
I went into this shell
- A nice, warm, safe shell.

00:11:31.737 --> 00:11:34.511
But lately, i've been thinking...

00:11:34.544 --> 00:11:38.151
It's not what she would
have wanted for me.

00:11:38.184 --> 00:11:39.653
So...

00:11:44.798 --> 00:11:46.100
So, what about you?

00:11:46.134 --> 00:11:48.839
You're a reasonably attractive guy.

00:11:50.510 --> 00:11:52.246
Reasonably.

00:11:52.279 --> 00:11:55.453
Why haven't you been out and about?

00:12:03.701 --> 00:12:07.410
Another long story for another time.

00:12:13.589 --> 00:12:15.459
So, she just handed the
providences over to you?

00:12:15.493 --> 00:12:16.662
Provenances.

00:12:16.694 --> 00:12:19.534
Provenances? Yes, we
went back to her place.

00:12:19.568 --> 00:12:21.872
I got a copy of the papers.

00:12:21.905 --> 00:12:23.375
And?

00:12:23.409 --> 00:12:26.648
And nothing. That's it. I left.

00:12:26.682 --> 00:12:31.057
You didn't have to con her
or do any special favors?

00:12:31.090 --> 00:12:33.094
Would you get your mind
out of the gutter, please?

00:12:33.127 --> 00:12:35.633
When this whole thing's done,
we could stick around a bit.

00:12:35.666 --> 00:12:37.403
Why? So you could take her out again.

00:12:37.437 --> 00:12:39.273
It's obvious you're into
her. Even i can see that.

00:12:39.306 --> 00:12:41.578
Hey, all right. I think
i got something here.

00:12:45.819 --> 00:12:47.624
"Portrait of isaiah merchant's family,

00:12:47.657 --> 00:12:48.993
Painted 1910."

00:12:49.026 --> 00:12:51.097
Now compare the names of the
owners with dad's journal.

00:12:55.405 --> 00:12:59.179
"First purchased in 1912 to peter sims."

00:12:59.213 --> 00:13:01.417
Peter sims murdered, 1912.

00:13:05.493 --> 00:13:08.131
Same thing in 1945.

00:13:08.164 --> 00:13:10.670
Oh, same thing in 1970.

00:13:10.703 --> 00:13:11.937
Then stored,

00:13:11.972 --> 00:13:14.310
Until it was donated to a
charity auction last month,

00:13:14.343 --> 00:13:16.213
Where the telescas bought it.

00:13:16.247 --> 00:13:18.918
So, what do you think?
It's haunted or cursed?

00:13:18.951 --> 00:13:21.123
Either way, it's toast.

00:13:43.535 --> 00:13:45.105
Go ahead.

00:14:29.928 --> 00:14:31.297
Ugly-Ass thing.

00:14:31.330 --> 00:14:34.203
If you ask me, we're doing
the art world a favor.

00:15:03.912 --> 00:15:06.182
We got a problem. I
can't find my wallet.

00:15:06.918 --> 00:15:08.688
How's that my problem?

00:15:08.722 --> 00:15:12.062
'Cause i think i dropped it
in the warehouse last night.

00:15:12.095 --> 00:15:13.097
You're kidding, right?

00:15:13.130 --> 00:15:14.834
I mean, it's got my prints, my i.D. -

00:15:14.867 --> 00:15:16.938
Well, my fake i.D.,
anyway, but we got to get it

00:15:16.971 --> 00:15:18.775
Before somebody else finds it. Come on.

00:15:29.062 --> 00:15:31.133
How do you lose your wallet, dean?

00:15:32.903 --> 00:15:34.740
Hey, guys.

00:15:34.774 --> 00:15:37.045
Sarah. Hey.

00:15:37.078 --> 00:15:38.647
What are you doing here?

00:15:38.681 --> 00:15:40.886
Oh...

00:15:40.919 --> 00:15:42.254
We're
- We're leaving town,

00:15:42.288 --> 00:15:44.392
And, you know, we came to say goodbye.

00:15:44.426 --> 00:15:46.230
What are you talking about, sam?

00:15:46.262 --> 00:15:49.069
We're sticking around for
at least another day or two.

00:15:49.102 --> 00:15:50.638
Oh, sam, by the way,

00:15:50.671 --> 00:15:54.079
I wanted to give you
that 20 bucks i owe you.

00:15:54.112 --> 00:15:57.418
I always forget.

00:15:57.452 --> 00:15:59.523
There you go.

00:16:02.228 --> 00:16:04.032
Well, i'll leave you
two crazy kids alone.

00:16:04.065 --> 00:16:06.670
I got to go do... something...somewhere.

00:16:13.919 --> 00:16:15.822
So...

00:16:15.856 --> 00:16:17.225
I had a good time last night.

00:16:17.258 --> 00:16:19.262
Yeah. Yeah, i did, too.

00:16:19.296 --> 00:16:22.268
Maybe we should do it again sometime?

00:16:24.338 --> 00:16:26.844
You know, i'd love to, i really would,

00:16:26.878 --> 00:16:28.681
But dean
- He was just screwing around.

00:16:28.714 --> 00:16:30.953
We really are taking off today.

00:16:30.986 --> 00:16:33.157
Oh. Oh.

00:16:33.190 --> 00:16:34.593
Now that's too bad.

00:16:34.626 --> 00:16:37.432
Oh, my god! What?

00:16:37.465 --> 00:16:38.868
The -

00:16:38.902 --> 00:16:40.504
That painting...

00:16:40.538 --> 00:16:42.742
Looks so good.

00:16:42.775 --> 00:16:46.083
If you can call that monstrosity good,

00:16:46.116 --> 00:16:47.852
Then, yeah, i guess.

00:16:47.886 --> 00:16:49.890
Sarah, what do you know
about that painting?

00:16:49.924 --> 00:16:52.128
Not much. Just that it creeps me out.

00:16:52.161 --> 00:16:53.597
We sold it to the telescas

00:16:53.631 --> 00:16:55.601
At a charity auction the
night they were murdered.

00:16:55.635 --> 00:16:58.140
And now you're just gonna sell it again?

00:16:58.173 --> 00:17:01.079
As much as my dad wants
to, no. I won't let him.

00:17:01.113 --> 00:17:03.050
I think it'd be in bad taste.

00:17:03.083 --> 00:17:04.853
Good, yeah. You know what? Don't. Don't.

00:17:04.886 --> 00:17:06.490
Make sure you don't, okay? Why?

00:17:06.523 --> 00:17:08.594
Don't tell me you're interested in that.

00:17:08.627 --> 00:17:10.464
No, god, no. Not in buying it, no.

00:17:10.498 --> 00:17:13.070
I got to go. I got to
take care of something.

00:17:13.103 --> 00:17:14.639
But, um, i will call you back.

00:17:14.673 --> 00:17:16.209
I will call you. I'll see you later.

00:17:16.243 --> 00:17:18.580
Wait, so you're not leaving tonight?

00:17:18.614 --> 00:17:22.088
No, i guess not. I'll see you.

00:17:24.092 --> 00:17:25.962
Okay.

00:17:28.067 --> 00:17:31.073
I don't understand, dean.
We burned the damn thing.

00:17:31.106 --> 00:17:33.177
Yeah, thank you, captain obvious.

00:17:33.210 --> 00:17:37.151
We just need to figure out
another way to get rid of it.

00:17:37.185 --> 00:17:38.287
Any ideas?

00:17:38.320 --> 00:17:39.556
Okay, all right.

00:17:39.589 --> 00:17:42.061
Well, um, in almost all the
lore about haunted paintings,

00:17:42.095 --> 00:17:43.831
It's always the painting's
subject that haunts them.

00:17:43.864 --> 00:17:45.634
Yeah? All right.

00:17:45.668 --> 00:17:48.140
So we need to figure out
everything there is to know

00:17:48.173 --> 00:17:50.911
About that creepy-Ass family
in that creepy-Ass painting.

00:17:50.945 --> 00:17:53.050
What were their names again?

00:17:54.085 --> 00:17:55.388
The isaiah merchant family, right?

00:17:55.421 --> 00:17:57.191
Yeah, that's right.

00:17:57.225 --> 00:18:00.698
I dug up every scrap of
local history i could find.

00:18:00.731 --> 00:18:02.735
So, uh, are you boys crime buffs?

00:18:02.769 --> 00:18:05.708
Kind of. Why do you ask?

00:18:05.741 --> 00:18:07.078
Well...

00:18:10.684 --> 00:18:12.622
Yes. Yeah, that sounds about right.

00:18:12.655 --> 00:18:14.225
The whole family was killed?

00:18:14.259 --> 00:18:16.997
It seems this isaiah, he
slits his kids' throats,

00:18:17.030 --> 00:18:19.034
Then his wife, then himself.

00:18:19.068 --> 00:18:22.842
Now, he was a barber by
trade. Used a straight razor.

00:18:22.875 --> 00:18:24.646
Why'd he do it?

00:18:24.679 --> 00:18:26.950
Well, let's look.

00:18:26.983 --> 00:18:28.987
Uh, "people who knew
him described isaiah

00:18:29.021 --> 00:18:30.958
"As having a stern
and harsh temperament,

00:18:30.991 --> 00:18:32.662
And controlled his
family with an iron fist."

00:18:32.695 --> 00:18:37.472
Wife, two sons, adopted daughter
- Yeah, yeah.

00:18:37.505 --> 00:18:39.943
There were whispers that the
wife was gonna take the kids

00:18:39.976 --> 00:18:43.851
And leave, which, of course,
you know, in that day and age...

00:18:43.884 --> 00:18:46.990
So instead, old man isaiah,
well, he gave them all a shave.

00:18:47.023 --> 00:18:47.992
Kkkch!

00:18:50.264 --> 00:18:52.201
Does it say what happened to the bodies?

00:18:52.235 --> 00:18:53.704
They were all cremated.

00:18:56.743 --> 00:18:58.447
Anything else? Yeah.

00:18:58.480 --> 00:19:01.386
Actually, i found a
picture of the family.

00:19:01.419 --> 00:19:03.190
It's right here somewhere.

00:19:03.223 --> 00:19:05.126
Right. Here it is.

00:19:13.243 --> 00:19:15.881
Hey, could we get a
copy of this, please?

00:19:15.915 --> 00:19:17.752
Sure.

00:19:21.860 --> 00:19:23.062
Dad...

00:19:23.095 --> 00:19:26.269
You promised you wouldn't
sell that painting.

00:19:26.303 --> 00:19:28.139
I know, sweetie, but evelyn's offered

00:19:28.172 --> 00:19:29.676
A persuasive amount of money.

00:19:29.708 --> 00:19:33.250
You're shameless, you know that?

00:19:33.283 --> 00:19:36.055
For that kind of money,
i can afford to be.

00:19:40.730 --> 00:19:42.734
Sam: i'm telling you,
man. I'm sure of it.

00:19:42.768 --> 00:19:45.274
The painting at the auction
house, dad is looking down.

00:19:45.307 --> 00:19:47.110
The painting here, dad's looking out.

00:19:47.143 --> 00:19:48.480
The painting has changed, dean.

00:19:48.513 --> 00:19:50.818
So you think that daddy dearest
is trapped in the painting,

00:19:50.851 --> 00:19:52.488
And he's handing out columbian neckties

00:19:52.521 --> 00:19:55.059
Like he did with his family?
Well, yeah, it seems like it.

00:19:55.093 --> 00:19:57.097
But if his bones are already dusted,

00:19:57.130 --> 00:19:58.934
Then how are we gonna stop him?

00:19:58.967 --> 00:20:00.304
Well, if isaiah's position changed,

00:20:00.337 --> 00:20:02.408
Then maybe some other things in
the painting changed, as well.

00:20:02.441 --> 00:20:03.810
It could give us some clues.

00:20:03.844 --> 00:20:05.113
Like a "da vinci code" deal?

00:20:06.181 --> 00:20:07.217
I don't know.

00:20:07.250 --> 00:20:09.822
I'm still waiting for
the movie on that one.

00:20:09.856 --> 00:20:11.926
Anyway, we got to get back
in and see that painting,

00:20:11.960 --> 00:20:13.997
Which is a good thing,
because you can get more time

00:20:14.031 --> 00:20:15.266
To crush on your girlfriend.

00:20:15.300 --> 00:20:17.538
Dude...enough already.

00:20:17.571 --> 00:20:19.575
What? "What?" Ever since we got here,

00:20:19.609 --> 00:20:21.680
You've been trying to
pimp me out to sarah.

00:20:21.713 --> 00:20:22.915
Just back off, all right?

00:20:22.948 --> 00:20:24.318
Well, you like her, don't you?

00:20:24.352 --> 00:20:26.021
All right, you like her. She likes you.

00:20:26.055 --> 00:20:27.591
You're both consenting adults.

00:20:27.625 --> 00:20:28.694
What's the point, dean?

00:20:28.727 --> 00:20:30.196
We'll just leave. We always leave.

00:20:30.229 --> 00:20:31.966
Well, i'm not talking
about marriage, sam.

00:20:32.000 --> 00:20:33.904
I don't get it. What do
you care if i hook up?

00:20:33.937 --> 00:20:35.808
Maybe you wouldn't be
so cranky all the time.

00:20:41.251 --> 00:20:43.957
Seriously, sam, this isn't
about just hooking up, okay?

00:20:43.990 --> 00:20:46.963
I think that this sarah
girl could be good for you.

00:20:49.368 --> 00:20:52.742
And i don't mean any
disrespect, but i'm -

00:20:52.775 --> 00:20:54.712
I'm sure that this is
about jessica, right?

00:20:55.714 --> 00:21:00.524
Now, i don't know what it's like
to lose somebody like that...

00:21:00.557 --> 00:21:02.428
But...

00:21:02.461 --> 00:21:04.465
I would think that she
would want you to be happy.

00:21:06.770 --> 00:21:09.809
God forbid, have fun once in a while.

00:21:09.842 --> 00:21:11.044
Wouldn't she?

00:21:15.721 --> 00:21:17.491
Yeah, i know she would.

00:21:22.501 --> 00:21:27.944
Yeah, you're right. Part
of this is about jessica.

00:21:27.978 --> 00:21:29.347
But not the main part.

00:21:29.381 --> 00:21:31.285
What's it about?

00:21:36.161 --> 00:21:37.430
Yeah, all right.

00:21:37.464 --> 00:21:40.436
Well, we still got to see that painting,

00:21:40.470 --> 00:21:43.844
Which means you still
got to call sarah, so...

00:21:56.401 --> 00:21:57.838
Sarah, hey. It's sam.

00:21:57.872 --> 00:21:59.709
Hey, hi.

00:21:59.742 --> 00:22:01.980
Good, good, yeah. What about you?

00:22:02.012 --> 00:22:04.752
Yeah, good. Good, really good. Smooth.

00:22:04.785 --> 00:22:07.290
So, uh
- So, listen.

00:22:07.323 --> 00:22:09.127
Me and my brother were thinking

00:22:09.160 --> 00:22:11.231
That maybe we'd like to come back in

00:22:11.265 --> 00:22:13.068
And look at the painting again.

00:22:13.102 --> 00:22:15.774
I think maybe we are
interested in buying it.

00:22:15.807 --> 00:22:16.976
Wait, what?

00:22:17.010 --> 00:22:20.116
Who'd you sell it to?

00:22:20.149 --> 00:22:22.655
Sarah, i need an address right now.

00:23:07.878 --> 00:23:09.014
Sam, what's happening?

00:23:09.046 --> 00:23:11.150
I told you you shouldn't have come.

00:23:14.692 --> 00:23:15.928
Hello, anybody home?!

00:23:15.961 --> 00:23:18.499
You said evelyn might be in
danger. What kind of danger?

00:23:18.532 --> 00:23:22.407
I can't knock this sucker
down. I got to pick it.

00:23:22.440 --> 00:23:24.979
What are you guys, burglars?

00:23:25.012 --> 00:23:26.315
I wish it was that simple.

00:23:26.348 --> 00:23:28.787
Look, you really should wait in the car.

00:23:28.820 --> 00:23:30.188
Ugh.

00:23:30.222 --> 00:23:31.692
The hell i will. Evelyn's a friend.

00:23:31.726 --> 00:23:32.761
Evelyn?

00:23:32.795 --> 00:23:34.364
Sam: evelyn!

00:23:39.274 --> 00:23:40.509
Evelyn?

00:23:51.064 --> 00:23:53.736
Evelyn?

00:23:53.770 --> 00:23:55.138
It's sarah blake.

00:23:55.171 --> 00:23:56.608
Are you all right?

00:23:56.642 --> 00:23:57.911
Sarah, don't! Sarah!

00:24:04.024 --> 00:24:06.728
Oh, my god! Oh, my god!

00:24:16.148 --> 00:24:18.920
Hey. You all right?

00:24:18.953 --> 00:24:20.356
No, actually.

00:24:20.389 --> 00:24:23.696
I just lied to the cops and told
them i went to evelyn's alone

00:24:23.729 --> 00:24:26.168
And found her like that.

00:24:26.200 --> 00:24:27.336
Thank you. Don't thank me.

00:24:27.370 --> 00:24:28.739
I'm about to call them right back

00:24:28.772 --> 00:24:30.609
If you don't tell me
what the hell is going on.

00:24:30.643 --> 00:24:32.113
Who's killing these people?

00:24:36.253 --> 00:24:37.824
"What."

00:24:37.858 --> 00:24:39.293
What?

00:24:39.326 --> 00:24:40.563
It's not "who."

00:24:40.596 --> 00:24:43.502
It's "what" is killing those people.

00:24:46.441 --> 00:24:49.013
Sarah, you saw that painting move.

00:24:49.047 --> 00:24:51.852
No.

00:24:51.886 --> 00:24:54.557
No, i was
- I was seeing things.

00:24:54.591 --> 00:24:55.927
It's impossible.

00:24:55.961 --> 00:24:57.630
Yeah, well, welcome to our world.

00:24:57.663 --> 00:25:00.904
Sarah, i know this sounds crazy...

00:25:00.937 --> 00:25:03.175
But we think that that
painting is haunted.

00:25:07.583 --> 00:25:09.087
You're joking.

00:25:13.394 --> 00:25:15.900
You're not joking.

00:25:15.934 --> 00:25:18.371
God, the guys i go out with.

00:25:18.404 --> 00:25:20.042
Sarah, think about it.

00:25:20.075 --> 00:25:23.749
Evelyn, the telescas
- They both had the painting.

00:25:23.782 --> 00:25:25.385
And there have been others before that.

00:25:25.418 --> 00:25:26.956
Wherever this thing goes, people die,

00:25:26.989 --> 00:25:29.359
And we're just trying to stop it...

00:25:29.393 --> 00:25:30.796
And that's the truth.

00:25:30.830 --> 00:25:35.706
Well, then, i guess you better show me.

00:25:35.739 --> 00:25:36.741
I'm coming with you.

00:25:36.775 --> 00:25:38.145
What? No.

00:25:38.178 --> 00:25:40.616
Sarah, no. You should just go home.

00:25:40.649 --> 00:25:43.322
This stuff can get dangerous, and

00:25:45.226 --> 00:25:47.230
And i don't want you to get hurt.

00:25:47.263 --> 00:25:49.133
Look, you guys are probably crazy,

00:25:49.167 --> 00:25:50.703
But if you're right about this,

00:25:50.736 --> 00:25:52.740
When me and my dad sold that painting,

00:25:52.773 --> 00:25:54.777
We might have got these people killed.

00:25:54.811 --> 00:25:57.783
I'm not saying i'm not scared,
'cause i am scared as hell,

00:25:57.817 --> 00:25:59.988
But i'm not gonna run and hide, either.

00:26:02.860 --> 00:26:04.731
So are we going or what?

00:26:04.764 --> 00:26:05.933
Sam

00:26:07.970 --> 00:26:09.307
Marry that girl.

00:26:12.313 --> 00:26:16.154
Uh... isn't this a crime scene?

00:26:16.187 --> 00:26:18.759
You've already lied to the
cops. What's another infraction?

00:26:37.930 --> 00:26:41.537
Aren't you worried that it's
gonna, you know, kill us?

00:26:41.570 --> 00:26:43.742
No, it seems to do its thing at night.

00:26:43.775 --> 00:26:45.212
I think we're all right in daylight.

00:26:50.255 --> 00:26:52.492
Sam, check it out.

00:26:52.525 --> 00:26:53.962
The razor
- It's closed in this one,

00:26:53.996 --> 00:26:55.966
But it's open in that one.
What are you guys looking for?

00:26:56.000 --> 00:26:57.737
If the spirit's changing
aspects of the painting,

00:26:57.770 --> 00:27:00.508
Maybe it's doing so for a reason.

00:27:00.541 --> 00:27:04.751
Hey, hey, look at this
- The painting in the painting.

00:27:09.494 --> 00:27:12.166
It looks like a crypt or
a mausoleum or something.

00:27:22.987 --> 00:27:24.223
"Merchant."

00:27:32.973 --> 00:27:35.645
This is the third
boneyard we've checked.

00:27:35.678 --> 00:27:38.919
This ghost is jerking us around.

00:27:38.952 --> 00:27:41.891
So, this is what you
guys do for a living?

00:27:41.925 --> 00:27:44.464
Not exactly.

00:27:44.497 --> 00:27:46.935
We don't get paid.

00:27:46.968 --> 00:27:49.540
Well, mazel tov.

00:27:51.143 --> 00:27:53.281
Over there.

00:28:28.250 --> 00:28:32.426
Okay, that right there is the
creepiest thing i've ever seen.

00:28:32.459 --> 00:28:35.298
It was sort of a tradition at the time.

00:28:35.332 --> 00:28:36.534
Whenever a child died,

00:28:36.568 --> 00:28:38.804
Sometimes they'd preserve
the kid's favorite toy

00:28:38.838 --> 00:28:41.644
In a glass case, put it next
to the headstone in the crypt.

00:28:47.288 --> 00:28:49.059
Notice anything strange here?

00:28:49.092 --> 00:28:50.562
Uh, where do i start?

00:28:50.596 --> 00:28:52.131
No, that's not what i mean.

00:28:52.165 --> 00:28:53.234
Look at the urns.

00:28:55.505 --> 00:28:57.443
Yeah, there are only four.

00:28:57.476 --> 00:28:59.680
Mom and the three kids.

00:28:59.714 --> 00:29:01.417
Daddy dearest isn't here.

00:29:03.688 --> 00:29:05.191
So where is he?

00:29:05.224 --> 00:29:07.829
Sarah: so, what exactly is
your brother doing in there?

00:29:07.862 --> 00:29:09.700
Searching county death certificates,

00:29:09.734 --> 00:29:12.305
Trying to find out what
happened to isaiah's body.

00:29:12.338 --> 00:29:13.942
How'd he even get in the door?

00:29:13.975 --> 00:29:18.384
Lying and subterfuge, mostly.

00:29:20.589 --> 00:29:23.894
You have a, um
- You have an eyelash on your...

00:29:23.928 --> 00:29:25.732
You have it right
- No. Uh, you know what?

00:29:27.802 --> 00:29:29.105
Do you mind if i -

00:29:29.139 --> 00:29:31.511
No. Okay.

00:29:31.544 --> 00:29:33.515
Okay, i got it.

00:29:33.548 --> 00:29:34.617
Make a wish.

00:29:42.865 --> 00:29:44.269
Sam, can i ask you something?

00:29:44.302 --> 00:29:46.940
Yeah, sure. I don't mean to be forward,

00:29:46.974 --> 00:29:51.651
But a girl could wait here forever.

00:29:51.684 --> 00:29:55.692
Is there something here
between us, or am i delusional?

00:29:55.726 --> 00:29:57.763
You're not delusional.

00:29:57.796 --> 00:30:00.868
But there's a "but" coming.

00:30:00.901 --> 00:30:03.974
But...

00:30:04.008 --> 00:30:06.581
I don't think this would be a good idea.

00:30:08.651 --> 00:30:09.787
Can i ask why?

00:30:11.858 --> 00:30:13.026
'Cause i like you.

00:30:15.431 --> 00:30:17.435
Wait. You lost me.

00:30:19.840 --> 00:30:22.579
Look, it's hard to explain.

00:30:22.613 --> 00:30:27.088
It's just that when
people are around me...

00:30:27.121 --> 00:30:28.858
I don't know, they get hurt.

00:30:28.892 --> 00:30:29.926
What do you mean?

00:30:29.959 --> 00:30:33.200
I mean, like, physically hurt.

00:30:33.233 --> 00:30:36.273
With what my brother and i do, it's...

00:30:41.751 --> 00:30:45.056
Sarah...

00:30:45.090 --> 00:30:47.060
I had a girlfriend.

00:30:48.464 --> 00:30:50.869
And she died.

00:30:50.902 --> 00:30:54.643
And my mom died, too.

00:30:54.677 --> 00:30:58.685
I don't know, it's like...

00:30:58.718 --> 00:31:01.924
It's like i'm cursed or something...

00:31:01.958 --> 00:31:03.560
Like death just follows me around.

00:31:03.594 --> 00:31:06.132
Look, i'm not scared of much,

00:31:06.166 --> 00:31:08.638
But if i let myself have
feelings for anybody -

00:31:08.671 --> 00:31:10.541
You're scared they get hurt, too.

00:31:12.445 --> 00:31:17.355
That's very sweet and very archaic.

00:31:17.388 --> 00:31:18.892
Sorry? Look, i'm a big girl, sam.

00:31:18.925 --> 00:31:21.363
It's not your job to
make decisions for me.

00:31:21.396 --> 00:31:23.701
There's always a chance of getting hurt.

00:31:23.735 --> 00:31:25.437
I'm not talking about a broken heart

00:31:25.471 --> 00:31:26.606
And a tub of haagen-Dazs.

00:31:26.640 --> 00:31:27.809
I'm talking about life and death.

00:31:27.843 --> 00:31:29.880
And tomorrow, i could get hit by a bus.

00:31:29.914 --> 00:31:31.016
That's what life is.

00:31:32.083 --> 00:31:35.457
Look, i know losing somebody you love
- It's terrible.

00:31:35.491 --> 00:31:40.034
You shut yourself off.
Believe me, i know.

00:31:40.066 --> 00:31:42.739
But when you shut out pain...

00:31:42.773 --> 00:31:44.977
You shut out everything else, too.

00:31:45.010 --> 00:31:48.584
Sarah, you don't understand.
The pain that i went through...

00:31:48.617 --> 00:31:53.159
I can't go through it again. I can't.

00:31:57.200 --> 00:31:58.838
Am i interrupting something?

00:31:58.871 --> 00:32:00.674
No. Not at all.

00:32:00.708 --> 00:32:02.078
Apparently.

00:32:02.110 --> 00:32:03.915
So, what'd you get? Pay dirt.

00:32:03.948 --> 00:32:07.355
Apparently, the surviving
relatives of the merchant family

00:32:07.388 --> 00:32:09.893
Were so ashamed of isaiah that
they didn't want him interred

00:32:09.927 --> 00:32:12.264
With the family, so they
handed him over to the county.

00:32:12.298 --> 00:32:14.369
The county gave him a pauper's funeral,

00:32:14.402 --> 00:32:15.805
Economy-Style.

00:32:15.839 --> 00:32:18.076
Turns out he wasn't cremated.
He was buried in a pine box.

00:32:18.110 --> 00:32:19.545
<i>So there are bones to burn.</i>

00:32:19.579 --> 00:32:21.984
There are bones to burn.
Tell me you know where.

00:32:35.678 --> 00:32:37.615
You guys seem to be

00:32:37.648 --> 00:32:39.752
Uncomfortably comfortable with this.

00:32:39.786 --> 00:32:44.294
Well...this isn't exactly
the first grave we dug.

00:32:44.328 --> 00:32:48.637
Still think i'm a catch?

00:32:50.074 --> 00:32:52.144
Think i got something.

00:33:18.262 --> 00:33:20.100
Dean: you been a real
pain in the ass, isaiah.

00:33:22.138 --> 00:33:23.774
Good riddance.

00:33:35.296 --> 00:33:37.034
Dean, keep the motor running.

00:33:37.067 --> 00:33:39.872
I thought the painting was harmless now.

00:33:39.906 --> 00:33:42.678
Better safe than sorry.
We're gonna bury the sucker.

00:33:42.711 --> 00:33:43.814
I want to come with you.

00:33:43.847 --> 00:33:45.450
Are you sure?

00:33:45.484 --> 00:33:47.188
Hey, hey, hey.

00:33:47.221 --> 00:33:49.792
I'll stay here. You go make your move.

00:33:49.826 --> 00:33:51.663
S- S-Sam,
i'm serious!

00:34:19.118 --> 00:34:21.421
Uh, sam...

00:34:21.455 --> 00:34:24.195
You're the expert on
all this ghost stuff.

00:34:24.228 --> 00:34:25.631
Is that painting supposed
to look like that?

00:34:28.169 --> 00:34:30.274
Where's the little girl?

00:34:32.811 --> 00:34:34.248
And the razor?

00:34:49.245 --> 00:34:51.950
Dean! Hey, is that you?!

00:34:51.983 --> 00:34:53.452
Dean: sammy, you all right?!

00:34:58.663 --> 00:35:00.267
Tell me you slammed the front door.

00:35:00.300 --> 00:35:02.003
No, it wasn't me. I think
it was the little girl.

00:35:02.036 --> 00:35:04.108
Girl? What girl? Yeah,
she's out of the painting.

00:35:04.141 --> 00:35:05.644
I think it might have
been her all along.

00:35:05.677 --> 00:35:07.013
Wasn't the dad looking down at her?

00:35:07.046 --> 00:35:08.482
Maybe he was trying to warn us.

00:35:08.515 --> 00:35:10.921
Hey, let's recap later.
Just get us out of here.

00:35:10.954 --> 00:35:13.760
I'm trying to pick the lock, and
the door won't budge. Break it down.

00:35:13.793 --> 00:35:16.766
Okay, genius, let me grab my battering
ram! Dean, the damn thing's coming!

00:35:16.799 --> 00:35:18.937
You're gonna have to hold it
off until i figure something out.

00:35:18.970 --> 00:35:20.941
Get some salt or iron.

00:35:24.080 --> 00:35:26.285
What kind of house doesn't have salt?

00:35:26.319 --> 00:35:28.790
Hey, you find any
iron? No, what's it for?

00:35:28.823 --> 00:35:30.694
Iron repels evil spirits,
but it's got to be pure.

00:35:30.727 --> 00:35:32.965
Hurry.

00:35:32.998 --> 00:35:36.571
Uh, dean, give me a
sec. Don't go anywhere.

00:35:36.605 --> 00:35:39.110
Look at a chair. Sometimes the seats...

00:35:58.015 --> 00:35:59.117
Sam!

00:36:17.053 --> 00:36:19.358
That is just so wrong.

00:36:40.800 --> 00:36:43.640
Iron?

00:36:43.672 --> 00:36:44.707
Yeah.

00:36:44.741 --> 00:36:47.079
Sam, are you okay?

00:36:47.113 --> 00:36:48.115
Yeah, for now.

00:36:48.148 --> 00:36:49.518
How we gonna waste her?

00:36:49.552 --> 00:36:51.322
I don't know. She was already cremated.

00:36:51.355 --> 00:36:53.593
There's nothing left to burn.
Well, then, how's she still around?

00:36:53.626 --> 00:36:54.995
There must be something else.

00:36:56.298 --> 00:36:57.800
Sam, wait.

00:36:57.834 --> 00:37:00.005
We used to handle antique
dolls at the auction.

00:37:00.039 --> 00:37:03.111
Well, that's fascinating,
sarah, but important right now?

00:37:03.145 --> 00:37:06.284
Back then, they used to make
the dolls in the kid's image.

00:37:06.318 --> 00:37:07.521
I mean, everything.

00:37:07.554 --> 00:37:09.992
Like, they would use
the kid's real hair.

00:37:10.025 --> 00:37:11.194
Dean?

00:37:11.228 --> 00:37:14.167
Sarah says the doll might
have the girl's hair.

00:37:14.200 --> 00:37:17.173
Human remains
- Same as bones.

00:37:17.206 --> 00:37:19.043
Both: the mausoleum.

00:37:47.867 --> 00:37:49.638
Sam!

00:38:14.688 --> 00:38:15.690
Come on, dean.

00:38:35.963 --> 00:38:37.900
Come on! Come on!

00:39:30.104 --> 00:39:31.341
Sam, you good?

00:39:35.482 --> 00:39:36.551
Not bad.

00:39:55.439 --> 00:39:57.878
This was archived in the county records.

00:39:57.911 --> 00:40:00.449
The merchant's adopted
daughter, melanie.

00:40:00.482 --> 00:40:02.051
Know why she was up for adoption?

00:40:02.085 --> 00:40:04.958
'Cause her real family
was murdered in their beds.

00:40:04.992 --> 00:40:06.227
She killed them?

00:40:06.261 --> 00:40:07.998
Yeah, who would suspect
her? A sweet little girl.

00:40:08.030 --> 00:40:10.235
So then she kills isaiah and his family.

00:40:10.269 --> 00:40:11.739
The old man takes the blame.

00:40:11.772 --> 00:40:13.976
His spirit's been trying
to warn people ever since.

00:40:14.010 --> 00:40:15.679
Where's this one go?

00:40:15.713 --> 00:40:17.316
Take it out back and burn it.

00:40:19.253 --> 00:40:22.727
I'm serious, guys. Thanks.

00:40:25.465 --> 00:40:27.603
So, why'd the girl do it?

00:40:27.636 --> 00:40:29.607
Killing others, killing herself -

00:40:29.640 --> 00:40:31.678
Some people are just born tortured.

00:40:31.711 --> 00:40:34.383
So when they die, their
spirits are just as dark.

00:40:34.417 --> 00:40:36.654
Maybe. I don't really care. It's over.

00:40:36.688 --> 00:40:39.327
We move on.

00:40:41.163 --> 00:40:42.767
I guess this means you're leaving.

00:40:49.547 --> 00:40:53.488
I'll go wait in the car. See you, sarah.

00:40:57.797 --> 00:40:59.968
I'm the one who burned the
doll and destroyed the spirit,

00:41:00.002 --> 00:41:01.203
But don't thank me or anything.

00:41:07.248 --> 00:41:10.589
There are a million things
that i want to say to you,

00:41:10.622 --> 00:41:13.528
But for the life of me,
i can't think of one.

00:41:13.561 --> 00:41:16.467
Yeah, i'll miss you, too.

00:41:16.501 --> 00:41:19.006
You know, there's a
lesson in all of this.

00:41:19.040 --> 00:41:20.042
What's that?

00:41:20.075 --> 00:41:22.680
We all got through this in one piece.

00:41:23.782 --> 00:41:25.385
I didn't get hurt.

00:41:25.419 --> 00:41:27.423
Yeah, i'm glad for that.

00:41:27.456 --> 00:41:30.829
So maybe you're not cursed.

00:41:30.863 --> 00:41:33.333
Maybe...

00:41:36.674 --> 00:41:39.146
Maybe you'll come back and see me.

00:41:42.820 --> 00:41:44.390
I will.

00:42:28.278 --> 00:42:30.916
That's my boy.

00:00:03.641 --> 00:00:05.144
